# Product Search Implementation: PHYTO.bg Catalog

Use this rule when implementing or modifying any part of the header search feature.

Use together with:
- `000-main-phyto-cursor-instructions.mdc`
- `selecta-phyto-catalog-project-context.mdc`
- `wordpress-acf-theme-instructions-updated.mdc`

## What this search is and is not

Search is a catalog lookup tool. It is not a commerce feature.

Search MUST:
- Return only `selecta_product` posts.
- Show product image, product line, title, and short benefit in results.
- Link each result to the single product detail page.
- Work entirely within WordPress native capabilities.
- Optionally show `product_score` (stars) and `product_price` in results when those ACF fields are set — same conditional display logic as the product card. These are catalog display fields only, not checkout or cart behaviour.

Search MUST NOT:
- Return or display add-to-cart, stock, discount badges, checkout, or any commerce action.
- Return posts from any other post type (pages, advice, partners, etc.).
- Use WooCommerce, Algolia, Upstash, Elasticsearch, SearchWP, Relevanssi, or any search plugin or external service.
- Use jQuery.
- Hardcode the REST URL in JavaScript.

## Stack decision

WordPress native only:
- PHP REST endpoint registered in `inc/search.php`.
- Search index stored as post meta (`_selecta_search_index`) on each product.
- Vanilla JS in `assets/js/search.js` (separate module, enqueued after `main.js`).
- Plain CSS in `assets/css/components/search-overlay.css`.
- REST URL localized via `wp_localize_script` on `selecta-main` in `inc/assets.php`; read by `search.js` as `window.selectaSearch`.

No search plugin. No external service. No build step.

